  "baseRefName": "main",
  "body": "## Accepted prior published result\n\nTarget 30005421 / OWR-12697690-001 is accepted as already proved by Markus Reineke, *Expander representations of quivers*, Theorem 2.4 (forward implication), [Forum of Mathematics, Sigma 14 (2026), e132](https://doi.org/10.1017/fms.2026.10284), published online 29 September 2026. The [author's v2](https://arxiv.org/abs/2411.15609v2) and the original question in [OWR 7/2023, printed pp.405\u2013406](https://ems.press/content/serial-article-files/47001) are credited. Reineke's acknowledgment of Urban Jezernik is preserved. Zero new substantive proof-search turns; no novelty claim.\n\nThe unchanged proof application and independent audit cover the complete original target: finite acyclic wild quivers over an algebraically closed field in any characteristic, including disconnected quivers. The slope is fixed and rational, with positive denominator on the full nonnegative cone. One unbounded family works for every cutoff, with a positive uniform gap along the family and strictness obtained by halving. No remaining bridge is identified for the stated target. No converse audit, nonclosed-field extension, oriented-cycle extension, arbitrary prescribed slope, explicit matrices, or gap uniformly positive as the cutoff tends to one is claimed.\n\n## Publication boundary and historical limitation\n\nOnly new files under `unsolved_math_prioritization/attempts/30005421/`: the unchanged proof application, unchanged independent audit and safe independent checker, acceptance/status, public-source metadata, and reproducibility evidence. No queue file or queue content is included or changed. Third-party source documents/text/images, dataset contents, private sources, private coordination files, the original assert-only checker and the full legacy archive are excluded. Draft only; no merge, release, DOI or external outreach.\n\nThe original checker's ten assertions disappear under Python -O/-OO. Its limitation report and original authored acceptance are preserved as historical metadata; historical optimized PASS is not treated as executed mathematical verification. The portable original assert-checker replay and full legacy-archive replay are NOT_RUN. Source records describe accepted earlier inspections, including the successful EMS PDF verification addendum; this packaging step does not claim new source-body retrieval or inspection.\n\n## Independent checker and fixed external trust anchor\n\nThe unchanged independent checker has zero assert nodes. Each clean run executes 323,049 explicit exact-arithmetic checks, enumerates 16,883 vectors, tests 1,386 eligible nonzero proper vectors and 7,919 strict cutoffs, and includes 634 negative-Rayleigh samples. Twelve semantic mutants are rejected with their exact expected reasons and full witnesses in each Python mode. These finite checks support the universal written proof; they do not prove its geometry or quantifiers by enumeration.\n\nAuthenticate BOOTSTRAP.py externally before running it. The fixed external bootstrap pins the verifier, controls harness and manifest. The manifest binds the whole remaining packet, including acceptance and preparation receipts. A candidate-supplied replacement manifest cannot replace the external trust anchor.\n\n- BOOTSTRAP.py SHA-256: `82049a7ea7548620fab8645336d23d4af9bdb103688572566994c3e47f0d07a2`\n- PUBLICATION_MANIFEST.json SHA-256: `818568f3c511421490a7dcf4acaa4345f4e8d8daf7c284ffc1a5f7cbf668a745`\n- verify_publication.py SHA-256: `29b85f54f231eaac3ffdb87b760c4f95084ebfd8435514cf00493161cb9819ad`\n- independent_check.py SHA-256: `6998e80dc02438275b775b0ee56c8c4c8b61ef1559f6baf62eebe7a9ed7e7cbe`\n\nFresh complete stdout/stderr match mode-specific pinned references exactly, with recursive exact JSON types and no normalization. The final external bootstrap tests ran in normal, -O and -OO with actual UID=EUID=1000, a 0555 directory, 0444 files, failed create/append probes, hostile-import tests, and explicit full before/after byte-count and SHA-256 maps:\n\n- normal: exit 0; 126 integrity negatives, 78 schema/scope negatives, 175 direct-comparator negatives; 110 actual EACCES denials; hostile baseline byte-identical. Full external receipt SHA-256: `7205dbecfcecfb25b45e9e1e134bc03615cdfe87512f886980a45020e8d23a88` (223069 bytes); stderr empty.\n- O: exit 0; 126 integrity negatives, 78 schema/scope negatives, 175 direct-comparator negatives; 110 actual EACCES denials; hostile baseline byte-identical. Full external receipt SHA-256: `2ccd64c92bc6f8aa3e4570cb7c8459e06efbbc255bfb4d0ab8751a8519dab4a1` (223069 bytes); stderr empty.\n- OO: exit 0; 126 integrity negatives, 78 schema/scope negatives, 175 direct-comparator negatives; 110 actual EACCES denials; hostile baseline byte-identical. Full external receipt SHA-256: `b07c28d3bf994c1f7b5d55ad358f362b4762a3131479cf9be7b4e6c8202e44b6` (223069 bytes); stderr empty.\n\nPREPARATION_CONTROLS_* and PREPARATION_RECEIPT.json explicitly describe the earlier pre-final-seal stage identified by PREPARATION_STAGE.json. The final manifest binds them; the final external receipts are outside the packet to avoid circular hashes. Source-body replay, dataset replay and formal proof-assistant verification are also NOT_RUN.\n\nThe ten workflows at the pinned base have no matching path filters. This is not a green-CI claim. Remote byte readback and exact-commit checks remain NOT_RUN until publication.\n",
